                "username": "eddiejames"
            },
            "createdOn": 1757446099,
            "author": {
                "name": "Edward A. James",
                "email": "eajames@linux.ibm.com",
                "username": "eddiejames"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we please be more precise here? Here's the change:\n\nhttps://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=b286f4e87e325b76789f30337c98ba72e00532e2\n\nThat's present from v6.8-rc1.\n\nCan you please add the link and update the subject?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Edward A. James",
                        "email": "eajames@linux.ibm.com",
                        "username": "eddiejames"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "console-server.c",
                    "line": 272,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not enthused by this, but I also don't like any alternatives I tried."
                },
                {
                    "file": "console-server.c",
                    "line": 272,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "I think the path resolution changes are unavoidable, and we don't have any easier options with handy symlinks within the sysfs tree.\n\nHowever, I'm not too keen on this fallback approach - it hides the two options of path resolution.\n\nPerhaps something like this: https://github.com/jk-ozlabs/obmc-console/blob/9639e633529e0ecd56a23363d1657100c2be4f9e/console-server.c#L217-L234\n\n\\- where the path configurations are explicit, and we just loop over those.\n\nFeel free to steal/squash from that [`experimental/vuart-sysfs`](https://github.com/openbmc/obmc-console/compare/master...jk-ozlabs:obmc-console:experimental/vuart-sysfs) branch, but note that it's just a sketch for this comment - I have not built nor tested)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "console-server.c",
                    "line": 272,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Edward A. James",
                        "email": "eajames@linux.ibm.com",
                        "username": "eddiejames"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks Jeremy! I took your commit and tested it, it works well. Thanks!"
                }
            ],
